                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]A simple match-tile game with farm animals, fruit, & veggies: each with a cute facial expression and matching sound effect. A Majong game for all ages.[/h1]\n\n[b]Audio/ Music:[/b]\nI not only enjoy the relaxing theme music, which reminds me of some of the themes in Disney Infinity, but I like the pleasing sounds the animals make when you find a match. There's a sound for running out of time that is not like a buzzer, but more of a sad melody. Little things like this add to the compulsion to keep flipping tiles, even when you miss. \n\n[b]Art/ Graphics:[/b] \nThere are 4 sets of 20 levels: 80 total on each of 8 maps, so quite a bit of play time with 640 levels. Flat 2d graphics, with nothing special, but nothing wrong. The different background images on each of the maps is neat and looks good. \n\n[b]Gameplay Mechanics:[/b]\nThe game opens each map with a mini-tutorial. It explains tile movement so a Majong beginner could understand at any age. When it said that the covered tiles were 'asleep,' I though that was a cute euphemism, but they were actually asleep. Clicking the wrong animal would give you a snoring sound and zzzzzz's. The quality of life adjustments in the game make it very playable. The gameplay flows smoothly. A dog will match any dog, and the same with cats and ducks. Rather than making the game easier, it gave a little more challenge because you had to find the non-matching same species creatures. \nBut, the real fun was with the 3d maps, where the tiles appeared on the rotatable sides of a rubiks cube-like field. Then no tiles were sleeping, and you had to rotate the cube to find matching tractors and windmills. \n\n[h1]There is a lot to offer in this low-priced game, which is currently on sale in the Summer sale. I recommend this for casual gamers of all ages who are looking for a relaxing way to pass the time.[/h1]",
